WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.333
Does a big context window give an agent memory?

2
00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:06.773
It doesn't, because the window starts empty each session,

3
00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:12.167
so AI memory management stores facts outside the model and decides what to forget.

4
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:13.767
When that store fills,

5
00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:19.067
least-recently-used eviction keeps recent small talk and drops the user's deployment region,

6
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.027
because recency has nothing to do with importance.

7
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:29.267
So I'd score each entry by its relevance to the task and by whether the user asked to remember it.

8
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:34.427
To start, I'd store session state explicitly and add eviction on day one,

9
00:00:34.427 --> 00:00:37.427
before a long customer session fills the context.
